          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorics"} combinatorics
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            %em hook-content formula
            expresses the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number"} number
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semistandard+Young+tableaux"} semistandard Young tableaux
            with fixed underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Young+diagram"} Young diagram
            and upper bound on its labels in terms of the “hook lengths” and the “content of boxes” of the underlying diagram.
          %p
            If the dependency in the “contents” is removed, the formula reduces to the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hook+length+formula"} hook length formula
            that counts
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Young+tableaux"} standard Young tableaux
            of the given shape.
          %p
            Both of these formulas equivalently give
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensions"} dimensions
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreps"} irreps
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
          %div
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hook+length+formula"} hook length formula
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hook-content+formula"} hook-content formula
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number"} number
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Young+tableaux"} standard Young tableaux
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number"} number
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semistandard+Young+tableaux"} semistandard Young tableaux
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreps"} irreps
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Specht+module"} of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} Sym(n)
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreps"} irreps
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SL%28n%29"} SL(n)
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hook+length+formula"} hook length formula
            for more on this.
          %h2#preliminaries Preliminaries
          %p
            Given a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Young+diagram"} Young diagram
            %em hook
            at any one of its boxes is the collection of boxes to the right and below that box, and including the box itself. We write “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℓ
                  %mi hook
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell hook
            ” for the
            %em length
            of such a hook, i.e. for the number of boxes it contains. Formally:
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (hook length)
              %br/
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ≥
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mrow
                        %mi rows
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi λ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda = (\lambda_1 \geq \cdots \geq \lambda_{rows(\lambda)})
              be a
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition"} partition
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Young+diagram"} Young diagram
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi rows
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi λ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \{1, \cdots, rows(\lambda)\}
                  ,
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi λ
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \in \{1, \cdots, \lambda_i\}
            %p
              the
              %em hook length
              at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,j)
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi hook
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi i
                    %mo −
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi λ
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi j
                    %mo −
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\ell hook(i,j)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    1 +
                    (\lambda_i - j) + (\lambda'_j - i)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda'
              denotes the
              %em conjugate partition
              (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Young+diagram#Conjugation"} there
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi i
                    %mo −
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_i - j
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi j
                    %mo −
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda'_j - i
              are commonly referred to as the
              %em arm length
              and
              %em leg length
              of box
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,j)
            %p
          %p Alongside this terminology one says that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi content
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi j
                  %mo −
                  %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  content(i,j)
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  j - i
                  \\;\;
                  \\in
                  \\mathbb{Z}
          %p
            is the
            %em content
            of the box
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,j)
          %p
            %br/
          %p Consider in the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ≥
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ≥
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mrow
                          %mi rows
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi λ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda = (\lambda_1 \geq \cdots \geq \lambda_{rows(\lambda)})
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition"} partition
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi λ
                          %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i}{\sum} \lambda_i = n
              %p
                equivalently a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Young+diagram"} Young diagram
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                boxes;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \in \mathbb{N}_+
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
          %p Write:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ssYT
                        %mi λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ssYT_\lambda(N)
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semistandard+Young+tableaux"} semistandard Young tableaux
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    of shape (i.e. with underlying
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Young+diagram"} Young diagram
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi λ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                %li
                  %p
                    with labels
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi T
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo ,
                              %mi j
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi N
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{i,j} \leq N
                    (i.e. with
                    = succeed ")." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ,
                                %mi j
                            %mo ∈
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo ,
                            %mi N
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{i,j} \in \{1, \cdots, N\}
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n(T) = \sum_{i,j} T_{i,j}
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
                of all the labels.
          %h2#statement Statement
          %h3#standard_hookcontent_formula Standard hook-content formula
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              a
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition"} partition
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Young+diagram"} Young diagram
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \in \mathbb{N}_+
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number"} number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %msub
                        %mi ssYTableaux
                        %mi λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left\vert ssYTableaux_\lambda(N)\right\vert
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semistandard+Young+tableaux"} semistandard Young tableaux
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              of shape
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              (
              %a{:href => "Schur+function#eq:SchurPolynomialCountsNumberOfSemiStandardYoungTableaux"} hence
              the value of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schur+polynomial"} Schur polynomial
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_\lambda
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              unit argument) and entries bounded by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{i,j} \leq N
              is:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %msub
                        %mi ssYTableaux
                        %mi λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi λ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi N
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo +
                        %mi content
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℓ
                        %msub
                          %mi hook
                          %mi λ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\vert ssYTableaux_\lambda(N)\right\vert
                    \\;=\;
                    s_{\lambda}
                    \\big(
                    x_1 \!=\! 1,
                    \\cdots,
                    x_N \!=\! 1
                    \\big)
                    \\;\;
                    \=
                    \\;\;
                    \\underset{
                    (i,j)
                    }{\prod}
                    \\frac{
                    N + content(i,j)
                    }{
                    \\ell hook_\lambda(i,j)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Stanley71"}> Stanley 71, Thm. 15.3
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Stanley99"} Stanley 99, Thm. 7.21.2
          %h3#deformed_hookcontent_formula
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            \-Deformed hook-content formula
          %p
            With the above ingredients, we have the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalities"} equalities
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomials"} polynomials
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variable"} variable
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi ssYT
                        %mi λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi i
                      %mi i
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mi i
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %mi rows
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi λ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi λ
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %msup
                        %mi q
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mo +
                          %mi content
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %msup
                        %mi q
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℓ
                          %mi hook
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{
                  T \in ssYT_\lambda(N)
                  }{\sum}
                  q^{ n(T) }
                  \\;\;=\;\;
                  q^{ \sum_i i \cdot \lambda_i }
                  \\cdot
                  \\!\!\!\!\!\!\!
                  \\underset{
                  { i \in \{1, \cdots, rows(\lambda)\} }
                  \\atop
                  {j \in \{1, \cdots, \lambda_i\}}
                  }{\prod}
                  \\frac{
                  1 - q^{N + content(i,j)}
                  }{
                  1 - q^{\ell hook(i,j)}
                  }
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Krattenthaler98"}> Krattenthaler 98, Thm. 1
            )
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hook+length+formula"} hook length formula
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Plancherel+measure"}> Plancherel measure
                ,
